<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahdia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahdia is a port city on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, built on a narrow peninsula. Founded in 916 by the first Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, Abdallah al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, it was the Fatimid capital until 948 and later the last stronghold of the Zirids after the Hilalian invasions. The Normans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> took it in 1148 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> in 1160, and Pisan, Genoese and French fleets attacked it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahdia.jpg" alt="Mahdia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davide Mauro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahdia_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1390 a French and Genoese expedition under Louis II, Duke of Bourbon, besieged <b>Mahdia</b> without success.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsid Sultanate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Under his admiral George of Antioch Sicilian fleets captured Tripoli in 1146 and <b>Mahdia</b> in 1148, creating a short-lived dominion on the North African coast known as the Kingdom of Africa, which the Almohads overran by 1160, and in 1147 raided Corfu, Thebes and Corinth.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sicily">Kingdom of Sicily · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Genoa was an old Ligurian port, squeezed between the Apennines and the sea, which had suffered Muslim raids in the tenth century and by the eleventh was raiding back, joining Pisa in attacks on Sardinia and on <b>Mahdia</b> in 1087.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Republic of Genoa · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Under Ali's brother Yahya ibn Ghaniya they took Tunis and <b>Mahdia</b> around 1203, devastating towns and countryside across Ifriqiya and Tripolitania.</blockquote><a href="/state/banu-ghaniya-of-ifriqiya">Banu Ghaniya of Ifriqiya</a></li><li><blockquote>His admiral George of Antioch took Tripoli in 1146, and in 1148 <b>Mahdia</b>, Sousse and Sfax fell as the Zirid ruler al-Hasan fled.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-africa">Kingdom of Africa</a></li><li><blockquote>Confined to <b>Mahdia</b> and the coast, the dynasty ended in 1148 when the Normans of the Kingdom of Africa took Mahdia.</blockquote><a href="/state/zirid-emirate">Zirid emirate</a></li></ul></section>
